                <pb facs="0889" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3839: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-23T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1922—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 23—2:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>230. Acting Minister of Finance yesterday summoned Reorganization Loan bankers to
                    enlist their support in raising $7,000,000 to meet various items of expenditure
                    which fall due Dragon Festival May 31st. He proposed issue treasury bonds
                    secured on salt surplus. They told him salt surplus was reserved for other
                    security by Presidential mandate of January last. Aforesaid bankers and their
                    ministers still considering matter.</p>
                <p>Correspondence published 21st between Chinese Bankers Association and Inspector
                    General Customs shows Government is using customs revenues for new expenditures
                    while customs surplus was already pledged to bankers as security for loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
